<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Dékhelé</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1886</span> · Also known as Battle of Dekhlé, Battle of Dékheulé</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Dékhelé was fought on 26 October 1886 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cayor">Cayor</a>, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal">Senegal</a>, between French colonial troops and the followers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lat-dior">Lat Dior Diop</a>, the former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damel">Damel</a> of Cayor. Lat Dior, who had long opposed the building of the Dakar–Saint-Louis railway across his country, was killed in the fighting. His death removed the last major <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolof">Wolof</a> resistance in Cayor, which was absorbed into French Senegal.</p></div>
